"Let $\\mathcal S$ be a finite set of finite connected graphs, and let $Ex^{\\bullet}(\\mathcal S)$ be the class of rooted, labelled or unlabelled, connected graphs with no minor in $\\mathcal S$. Let $R_n$ be a uniformly random element of $Ex^{\\bullet}(\\mathcal S)$ with $n$ vertices.\n\n**Rooted minor-exclusion convergence conjecture.** The sequence $R_n$ converges weakly.\n\nThis is an early formulation of the paper's main question. The paper proves the analogous convergence for important special cases, including subcritical classes, while the general minor-closed case remains open in this formulation."